# Licence

This directory is not under a single licence. Which licence applies depends on the
path:

| Path | Licence | Copyright |
|---|---|---|
| `patch/0002-zf8-tag-build.patch`, `patch/0003-zf8-kernel-side.patch` | GPL-2.0-only | upstream kernel-side contributors, plus the changes in those patches |
| `patch/0001-zf8-device.patch` | mixed, see below | |
| `artifacts/kernelsu-zf8-rc3-officialkey.ko` | GPL-2.0-only | built only from `kernel/` sources and kernel headers |
| `tools/`, `config/`, `build.sh`, `README.md`, `NOTICE` | GPL-2.0-only | written for this project, to match the module they serve |

Texts: [`LICENSE.GPL-2.0`](LICENSE.GPL-2.0), [`LICENSE.GPL-3.0`](LICENSE.GPL-3.0),
[`LICENSE.Linux-syscall-note`](LICENSE.Linux-syscall-note).

## Why the split

ReSukiSU is published under two licences at once. The repository root `LICENSE` is
GPL-3.0; `kernel/LICENSE` is GPL-2.0 and covers everything under `kernel/`. The
module is compiled from `kernel/` only, against kernel headers that are
GPL-2.0-only under the Linux syscall note. Nothing GPL-3.0 goes into it, so it is
GPL-2.0-only.

`0002` and `0003` touch only `kernel/` and kernel files, so they are GPL-2.0-only
and carry `SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only`.

`0001` is the exception: its hunks are mostly against `kernel/`, but one is against
`manager/app/src/main/java/com/resukisu/resukisu/data/kernel/KernelRepository.kt`,
which is under the repository root and therefore GPL-3.0. The kernel hunks are
GPL-2.0-only and the Kotlin hunk is GPL-3.0; the file is offered as-is for
convenience, and either half can be taken under its own terms.

The manager APK is not distributed here. It is built from `userspace/` and
`manager/`, both under the ReSukiSU repository root, and remains GPL-3.0 under
that project's terms; take it from their release page.
